 dictionary such as the Oxford Advanced Learner''s, Longman, or Cambridge would genuinely have nothing for this slot, so leaving it empty is complete. For example:\n- months, days, and numbers have no common collocations or synonyms beyond the names of their set\n- an uncountable noun (\"advice\") has no plural\n- a non-gradable adjective (\"main\", \"dead\") has no comparative\n- a function word or a general word (\"thing\", \"get\") belongs to no topic\nfail when the slot plainly applies to this word, so a learner would expect it filled, or the reason is wrong. For example:\n- a common verb lacks inflections, or a noun its plural, that a learner can look up in any dictionary\n- a word with ordinary synonyms, collocations, or a topic only someone has not found yet\n- a reason that is wrong, vague, or only says the data is hard to find\nuncertain: only when you cannot judge the word at all.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (adjective) \"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable.\"\n- (adjective) \"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought.\"\n- (adjective) \"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand.\"\n- (adjective) \"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest.\"\n- (adjective) \"Sexually attractive.\"\n- (adjective) \"Feeling strong sexual desire.\"\n- (adjective) \"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very skilful at a particular activity or knowledgeable about a particular subject.\"\n- (adjective) \"Newly obtained or produced and very recent.\"\n- (adjective) \"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very interested in or eager for something.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very likely to win or succeed.\"\n- (adjective) \"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed.\"\n- (adjective) \"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock.\"\n- (adjective) \"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very bright and strong in colour.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"hot","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game.","siblings":[{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Sexually attractive."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Feeling strong sexual desire."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very skilful at a particular activity or knowledgeable about a particular subject."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Newly obtained or produced and very recent."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very interested in or eager for something."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very likely to win or succeed."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very bright and strong in colour."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T13:05:21.380Z"}', '2026-11-10T13:05:10.449Z', '2026-11-10T13:05:21.380Z', NULL);
