r set\n- an uncountable noun (\"advice\") has no plural\n- a non-gradable adjective (\"main\", \"dead\") has no comparative\n- a function word or a general word (\"thing\", \"get\") belongs to no topic\nfail when the slot plainly applies to this word, so a learner would expect it filled, or the reason is wrong. For example:\n- a common verb lacks inflections, or a noun its plural, that a learner can look up in any dictionary\n- a word with ordinary synonyms, collocations, or a topic only someone has not found yet\n- a reason that is wrong, vague, or only says the data is hard to find\nuncertain: only when you cannot judge the word at all.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"A living creature that feeds on organic matter and typically can move and respond to its surroundings, including humans but excluding plants.\"\n- (noun) \"A creature other than a human, especially a mammal rather than a bird, fish, or insect.\"\n- (noun) \"A person who behaves in a cruel, violent, or uncivilized way.\"\n- (adjective) \"Relating to animals or derived from animals.\"\n- (adjective) \"Relating to physical appetites and instincts rather than reason or spiritual qualities.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"animal","pos":"noun","gloss":"A person or thing of a particular type.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A living creature that feeds on organic matter and typically can move and respond to its surroundings, including humans but excluding plants."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A creature other than a human, especially a mammal rather than a bird, fish, or insect."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person who behaves in a cruel, violent, or uncivilized way."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Relating to animals or derived from animals."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Relating to physical appetites and instincts rather than reason or spiritual qualities."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T07:46:31.359Z"}', '2026-11-10T07:30:23.126Z', '2026-11-10T07:46:31.359Z