arner''s, Longman, or Cambridge would mark it?\nIt claims the word in this sense is:\n- used both before a noun (\"a big house\") and after a linking verb such as \"be\" (\"the house is big\")\n- commonly followed by the preposition \"at\"\n- commonly followed by the preposition \"on\"\nJudge each claim for this sense only, never for another sense of the word.\nA named preposition claims that learners use that preposition after the word in this sense, as a learner''s dictionary writes it (\"rely on/upon sb/sth\", \"good at sth\").\npass: every claim holds for this sense. Patterns and prepositions are the common ones a learner needs, not all of them: a pattern or preposition left out is not an error.\nfail: any claim is wrong for this sense or holds only for another sense, a pattern is rare or unnatural with this sense, or a named preposition is not the one learners use with this sense or is rare with it.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (adjective) \"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable.\"\n- (adjective) \"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game.\"\n- (adjective) \"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand.\"\n- (adjective) \"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest.\"\n- (adjective) \"Sexually attractive.\"\n- (adjective) \"Feeling strong sexual desire.\"\n- (adjective) \"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell.\"\n- (adjective) \"Newly obtained or produced and very recent.\"\n- (adjective) \"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very interested in or eager for something.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very likely to win or succeed.\"\n- (adjective) \"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed.\"\n- (verb) \"To become more lively, exciting, or intense.\"\n- (adjective) \"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock.\"\n- (adjective) \"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very bright and strong in colour.\""}}}]},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"hot","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very skilful at a particular activity or knowledgeable about a particular subject.","siblings":[{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Sexually attractive."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Feeling strong sexual desire."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Newly obtained or produced and very recent."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very interested in or eager for something."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very likely to win or succeed."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To become more lively, exciting, or intense."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very bright and strong in colour."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T09:15:42.754Z"}', '2026-11-10T08:58:29.827Z', '2026-11-10T09:15:42.754Z', NULL);
