ims the word in this sense is:\n- transitive only: it takes a direct object and is not used without one\n- commonly followed by the preposition \"out of\"\nJudge each claim for this sense only, never for another sense of the word.\nA named preposition claims that learners use that preposition after the word in this sense, as a learner''s dictionary writes it (\"rely on/upon sb/sth\", \"good at sth\").\npass: every claim holds for this sense. Patterns and prepositions are the common ones a learner needs, not all of them: a pattern or preposition left out is not an error.\nfail: any claim is wrong for this sense or holds only for another sense, a pattern is rare or unnatural with this sense, or a named preposition is not the one learners use with this sense or is rare with it.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"An animal that lives in water, breathes through gills, and has fins.\"\n- (verb) \"To try to catch fish.\"\n- (verb) \"To try indirectly to obtain something from someone.\"\n- (noun) \"The flesh of fish eaten as food.\"\n- (verb) \"To search for something by feeling around with the hands.\"\n- (noun) \"A person of a particular kind or character.\""}}}]},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"fish","pos":"verb","gloss":"To pull or take something out of a place, especially with difficulty.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"An animal that lives in water, breathes through gills, and has fins."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To try to catch fish."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To try indirectly to obtain something from someone."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"The flesh of fish eaten as food."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To search for something by feeling around with the hands."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person of a particular kind or character."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T03:34:22.867Z"}', '2026-11-10T03:34:16.300Z', '2026-11-10T03:34:22.867Z', NULL);
