 noun or verb sense, an equivalent does not work as that part of speech.\n- It renders a phrase or phrasal verb that contains the word instead of the word in this sense.\n- It renders a different sense of the word, such as one of the other senses listed below.\n- It is unnatural or ungrammatical in the target language.\n- It lists equivalents of several unrelated senses.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"A small domesticated animal with soft fur, whiskers, and retractable claws, often kept as a pet.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"cat","pos":"noun","gloss":"A wild animal of the same family as the domestic cat, including lions, tigers, and leopards.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A small domesticated animal with soft fur, whiskers, and retractable claws, often kept as a pet."}]},"target":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-09T08:45:19.713Z"}', '2026-11-09T08:45:13.707Z', '2026-11-09T08:45:19.713Z', NULL);
