 when the slot plainly applies to this word, so a learner would expect it filled, or the reason is wrong. For example:\n- a common verb lacks inflections, or a noun its plural, that a learner can look up in any dictionary\n- a verb with common phrasal verbs the reason leaves out (\"throw\" has throw away, throw out, and throw up), or a word with common derivatives (\"happy\" has happiness)\n- a word with ordinary synonyms, collocations, or a topic only someone has not found yet\n- a reason that is wrong, vague, or only says the data is hard to find\nA fail reason names the specific value a learner''s dictionary gives for the slot, never only that one exists.\nReview already rejected these attempts to fill this slot, most recent first:\n- topic {\"topic_id\":\"biology\"} (topic \"Biology\" (in the category \"Science and technology\")): rejected because \"This sex-specific animal term is characteristic of breeding and animal husbandry rather than core vocabulary for studying biology.\"\n- topic {\"topic_id\":\"pets\"} (topic \"Pets\" (in the category \"Animals and plants\")): rejected because \"This sex-specific sense belongs to animal breeding terminology rather than core pets vocabulary, which uses the general animal sense of \\\"dog\\\".\"\nEach was judged not to fit. Never fail for a value one of them tried, or for an association as loose as theirs: when the attempts were rejected as not fitting, pass unless you can name a specific value that plainly fills the slot and differs from every rejected one.\nuncertain: only when you cannot judge the word at all.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"A domesticated animal with four legs, a tail, and a barking voice, often kept as a pet or trained for work.\"\n- (noun) \"A person, especially a man, regarded as unpleasant or contemptible.\"\n- (noun) \"Something of very poor quality or something that is a commercial failure.\"\n- (verb) \"To follow someone closely and persistently.\"\n- (verb) \"To cause persistent trouble or difficulty for someone or something.\"\n- (noun) \"A woman considered physically unattractive.\"\n- (noun) \"A man described in a familiar or affectionate way as having a particular quality.\"\n- (noun) \"A person''s feet.\"\n- (noun) \"A hot dog.\"\n- (noun) \"Greyhound racing, especially as an activity involving betting.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"dog","pos":"noun","gloss":"A male dog or a male of a related animal such as a fox.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A domesticated animal with four legs, a tail, and a barking voice, often kept as a pet or trained for work."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person, especially a man, regarded as unpleasant or contemptible."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"Something of very poor quality or something that is a commercial failure."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To follow someone closely and persistently."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To cause persistent trouble or difficulty for someone or something."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A woman considered physically unattractive."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A man described in a familiar or affectionate way as having a particular quality."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person''s feet."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A hot dog."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"Greyhound racing, especially as an activity involving betting."}]},"target":null,"topic":null,"attempts":[{"kind":"topic","payload":{"topic_id":"biology"},"word":null,"other":null,"topic":{"category":"Science and technology","topic":"Biology"},"reason":"This sex-specific animal term is characteristic of breeding and animal husbandry rather than core vocabulary for studying biology."},{"kind":"topic","payload":{"topic_id":"pets"},"word":null,"other":null,"topic":{"category":"Animals and plants","topic":"Pets"},"reason":"This sex-specific sense belongs to animal breeding terminology rather than core pets vocabulary, which uses the general animal sense of \"dog\"."}]},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T18:23:14.059Z"}', '2026-11-10T18:23:07.780Z', '2026-11-1