 one of these holds:\n- Complete: common has every common, general-knowledge sense a learner''s dictionary lists for this word, in every part of speech it has. A missing common sense fails.\n- Distinct: no two common senses are duplicates, or one meaning split too finely into several.\n- Ordered: common runs from the most to the least common use of the word.\n- Rare: every sense in extra is genuinely rare, archaic, technical, or specialist, not one a learner meets in general use.\nA rare, archaic, Old English, technical, or specialist sense missing from both lists is never a failure.\nfail when any of them does not hold. The reason then names everything to change, even if that takes more than one sentence: each missing common sense with its part of speech and a short meaning, each pair of duplicates by number, each sense out of order, and each sense in extra that is common.\nuncertain: you cannot tell."}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"cold","senses":[{"id":"875d6bbb-3ead-41d9-b8e4-d43e63b2cb31","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a low temperature or a temperature lower than is comfortable."},{"id":"e6dcbab9-b731-4292-bb4f-bda1b87dccb0","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Feeling a lack of warmth in the body."},{"id":"aae01623-0719-4ab6-a262-c21855f934e4","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Served without being heated or after being allowed to cool."},{"id":"406acb7f-7a73-4141-b9d2-039b09e24a3e","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Showing little affection, sympathy, or friendliness."},{"id":"261225b3-913d-4faa-9b6d-15a8017c4fa1","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Based on facts and reasoning without the influence of emotion."},{"id":"dd179a38-e400-447b-bbd2-a05f3cd32ce8","pos":"adjective","gloss":"No longer fresh enough to provide useful clues about someone or something being sought."},{"id":"456aaa0d-4384-4a7a-9dec-d4f2c2d0ff23","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Far from finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game."},{"id":"6a349b46-12c0-40ec-a085-e09dcb75b7e2","pos":"adjective","gloss"