n (\"advice\") has no plural\n- a non-gradable adjective (\"main\", \"dead\") has no comparative\n- a function word or a general word (\"thing\", \"get\") belongs to no topic\nfail when the slot plainly applies to this word, so a learner would expect it filled, or the reason is wrong. For example:\n- a common verb lacks inflections, or a noun its plural, that a learner can look up in any dictionary\n- a word with ordinary synonyms, collocations, or a topic only someone has not found yet\n- a reason that is wrong, vague, or only says the data is hard to find\nuncertain: only when you cannot judge the word at all.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"An animal with feathers, wings, and a beak that lays eggs and is usually able to fly.\"\n- (noun) \"A person of a particular type or character.\"\n- (noun) \"A shuttlecock used in badminton.\"\n- (noun) \"Time spent in prison.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"bird","pos":"noun","gloss":"A girl or young woman.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"An animal with feathers, wings, and a beak that lays eggs and is usually able to fly."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person of a particular type or character."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A shuttlecock used in badminton."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"Time spent in prison."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T08:29:57.832Z"}', '2026-11-10T08:11:23.086Z', '2026-11-10T08:29:57.832Z', NULL);
